---
import Scene from "@openducktor/product-scenes/astro";
import FeatureGrid from "../ui/FeatureGrid.astro";
import FeatureTile from "../ui/FeatureTile.astro";
import SectionHead from "../ui/SectionHead.astro";
---

<section id="oversight" class="section oversight" aria-labelledby="oversight-title">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <SectionHead eyebrow="Usage and processes" id="oversight-title">
      <Fragment slot="title">See what your agents use, and what they leave running.</Fragment>
      <p>
        Usage shows the tokens and the estimated cost of your agents. Processes shows the commands
        that they leave running. Open Usage from the sidebar, and Processes from the workspace rail.
      </p>
    </SectionHead>
    <FeatureGrid>
      <FeatureTile
        id="oversight-usage"
        label="Usage"
        title="The tokens and the estimated cost of every agent, in one place."
        size="full"
      >
        The Usage page reads the history of Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Antigravity on your
        computer. It also counts the sessions that you started outside OpenDucktor. Compare the
        runtimes, the models, and the projects of a range, and switch from tokens to cost. The cost
        is an estimate at API rates, not a bill.
        <Scene name="usage" slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="oversight-processes"
        label="Processes"
        title="Find the dev server that an agent left running, and stop it."
        size="full"
      >
        The Processes button of the rail counts the commands that run in your checkouts. The list
        shows the folder, the command, and its ports. Stop ends a command and each process that it
        started. Detach the list into a window that stays open on every page.
        <Scene name="processes" slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
    </FeatureGrid>
  </div>
</section>
